course: dictionary
lesson: 12620
title: Dislocated: out of its place
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Dislocated» comes from «dislocate», which means to push something out of its normal place. The word has two main meanings. The first is about the body: a bone pushed out of its joint. The second is about things that have been moved or broken up so they no longer work smoothly.
explain: «Sam fell off his bike, and his shoulder was dislocated.» The clue is the fall and the word shoulder. A shoulder is a joint, and a joint that has been hurt and knocked out of place is painful, so dislocated must mean pushed out of its normal place. This is a job for a doctor, not for a quick fix at home.
explain: «The storm dislocated the whole village, and families had to find new homes.» Here the clues are storm and families had to find new homes. People were moved from their usual places, so dislocated means forced out of their usual places. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Dislocate: dislocates, dislocated, dislocating. «Dislocated» is the past form and also an adjective, as in «a dislocated shoulder».
fact: A joint is the place where two bones meet, like your knee, elbow, finger or shoulder.
fact: «Dislocated» means pushed out of its normal place, especially a bone pushed out of its joint.
fact: «Dislocated» can also mean moved from its usual place, or broken up so it does not work smoothly, like «dislocated plans».
fact: A dislocated joint is painful and needs a doctor. Never try to push a bone back into place yourself.
exercise: «Sam fell off his bike, and his shoulder was dislocated.» What does dislocated mean here? | Painted bright red | Covered in a bandage | *Pushed out of its normal place in the joint | Very tired after a long ride
exercise: «The storm dislocated the whole village, and families had to find new homes.» What does dislocated suggest here? | *Forced out of their usual places | Given a prize | Cleaned and painted | Made the village bigger
exercise: Which of these is a body part that can be dislocated? | *a finger | a puddle | a cloud | a song
test: «The dislocated plans meant the trip was cancelled.» What does dislocated mean in this sentence? | Going very fast | *Broken up, so they no longer worked smoothly | Painted in bright colours | Made of wood
test: «Many families were dislocated by the flood.» What happened to the families? | *They were forced out of their usual homes | They won a prize | They went on holiday | They were given new cars
exam: «Ben's knee was dislocated during the football match.» Which meaning fits best? | Bright and shiny | *Pushed out of its normal place in the joint | Happily stretched out | Covered in mud
